# ===== Private output of the autonomous agency =====
# The loop GENERATES these two trees: every cycle writes a new strategy .py
# plus a _backtest_results.json and an _evaluation.json, named
# <Concept>_<YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS>. They are the operator's private working
# material, not source, and they are already in the thousands
# (2525 + 1677 files, ~32 MB) while the tracked source in
# autonomous_agency/ is 22 files. Never track them.
#
# A trailing slash matters here: it matches directories only, so a same-named
# .py at the repo root stays trackable. Leading slash anchors the pattern to
# the repo root, so a nested second copy is NOT silently covered.
#
# Ignoring does not untrack. Both rules were already present, yet 1279 files
# stayed in the index because they had been added before the rule existed
# (git only applies .gitignore to files it is not already tracking). They were
# removed with `git rm -r --cached`, which drops the index entry and leaves
# the file on disk. If a tree ever gets re-added by accident, the same
# command fixes it.
/autonomous_agency/strategies/
/autonomous_agency/results/
